```java
try (Statement st = con.createStatement(
         ResultSet.TYPE_SCROLL_INSENSITIVE, ResultSet.CONCUR_READ_ONLY);
     ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery("SELECT id FROM users")) {
    rs.last();                 // jump to last row
    int total = rs.getRow();   // row count
    rs.absolute(5);            // jump to row 5
    rs.previous();             // move backward
}
```

*Scrollable enables backward/random navigation but costs more memory; pick it only when needed.*

```java
record User(long id, String name, String email) {}

// RowMapper: maps ONE row to a User
interface RowMapper<T> { T map(ResultSet rs) throws SQLException; }
RowMapper<User> userMapper = rs ->
    new User(rs.getLong("id"), rs.getString("name"), rs.getString("email"));

List<User> users = new ArrayList<>();
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("SELECT id, name, email FROM users");
     ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {
    while (rs.next()) users.add(userMapper.map(rs));  // reuse the mapper
}
// Spring: jdbcTemplate.query("SELECT ... ", (rs, rowNum) -> new User(...));
```

