ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();
while (rs.next()) { process(rs); }  // if process() throws, rs never closes
rs.close();                          // skipped on exception -> leak
ps.close();
```

```java
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users");
     ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {
    while (rs.next()) { process(rs); }
}  // rs (then ps) auto-closed even if process() throws -> no cursor leak
```

*The cursor is released deterministically — don't wait for GC or hope the Statement closes it.*

```java
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(anySql);
     ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {
    ResultSetMetaData md = rs.getMetaData();
    int cols = md.getColumnCount();
    while (rs.next()) {
        StringBuilder row = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 1; i <= cols; i++) {            // 1-based
            row.append(md.getColumnLabel(i))         // header name
               .append('=').append(rs.getObject(i)).append(' ');
        }
        System.out.println(row);
    }
}
// works for ANY query without knowing its columns in advance
```

